# CODEOWNERS — protection for security-relevant surfaces.
#
# The repository is PUBLIC. GitHub treats a CODEOWNERS entry as a required
# reviewer when branch protection enables "Require review from Code Owners"
# (Settings → Branches → main; documented in deploy/README.md § CI trust
# boundary).
#
# Trust rule in force (v0.15): the nightly live-model evaluation job runs on
# a SELF-HOSTED runner and is schedule-only. It must never execute
# pull-request workflow code. These ownership rules keep any change that
# could alter that boundary (workflows, sandbox image, deployment surface)
# behind explicit owner review.

# Workflow files can change what executes on runners — always owner-reviewed.
